0035: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
0036:     """
0037:     Stamp the unique template mask into every divider-grid cell, recolored by each row's left marker.
0038: 
0039:     Input structure
0040:     - The background is the dominant color.
0041:     - One non-background color forms full horizontal and vertical divider bars, splitting the grid into equal-size cells.
0042:     - In the first column of cells, each row has a single-color marker that gives that row's output color.
0043:     - Exactly one non-first-column cell contains the single-color template mask to copy.
0044: 
0045:     Rule
0046:     - Read the row color from the marker in the first cell of each row band.
0047:     - Read the template as the non-background mask in the unique template cell.
0048:     - Clear every cell interior to background, then paint the template mask into every cell of a row using that row's marker color.
0049:     - Leave the divider bars unchanged.
0050: 
0051:     Key insight
0052:     - The visible colors are not copied as objects; the first column supplies a row palette and the lone extra cell supplies the shape mask.
0053:     """
